[[2047,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/3238857\">7045A10</a></p><p>1. Remove the rod springs.</p><p>2. Remove the lever.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2019346.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Make sure that the lever is\nnot damaged.</p><p>Reinstall the lever.</p><p>Install the rod springs.</p><p><a href=\"#/3238857\">7045A10</a></p><p>Check the functioning of the lever and\nthe correct sliding and hooking of the seat.</p>"]]